  "summary": "A technique creating tonal values through patterns of dots rather than lines.",
  "description": "Uses precise placement of dots to build up value, with closer dots creating darker areas and sparser dots creating lighter ones. Developed as an alternative to hatching, particularly favored for its ability to create smooth tonal transitions and avoid the directional bias of line-based techniques.",
